.TH AGENT-HOOK-POST-BASH 1 "2026-06-30" "agentguard" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agent-hook-post-bash \- check agent shell commands and output after execution
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agent-hook-post-bash
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B agent-hook-post-bash
reads an agent hook JSON payload from standard input, extracts command stdout
from known agent payload shapes, and warns when output appears to contain
high-confidence credentials such as private keys or common API token formats.
.PP
After a successful
.B git push
or
.BR "gh pr create" ,
.BR ready ,
.BR reopen ,
or
.BR update-branch ,
or output showing a push summary or a new pull-request URL (from any GitHub
host), it reminds the agent once per prompt that the pull request is not done
until its checks pass on the pushed commit, recommending
.B AGENTGUARD_PR_WATCH_HINT
when set, else
.B git pr-watch \-\-wait
when
.B git-pr-watch
is on
.BR PATH ,
else
.BR "gh pr checks \-\-watch" .
.BR "git pr-open" ,
.BR "git pr-submit" ,
.BR "git pr-restack" ,
and
.B git pr-sync-stack
count as pushes too.
.PP
When
.B git-pr-watch
is on
.BR PATH ,
a successful pull-request creation that prints the pull request's URL also
records it as a watch obligation for the session, and a later successful push
or
.B gh pr ready|reopen|update-branch
re-arms recorded ones; the reminder then recommends
.B git pr-watch \-\-wait
with their URLs. A successful
.B gh pr close
or
.B gh pr merge
(with a merge method and without
.BR \-\-auto )
that names a recorded pull request by URL or number forgets it, so nothing
waits for a watcher; a later reopen revives it.
.BR agent-hook-stop (1)
checks the obligations. The rules, including when a merge or close forgets
and the gaps, are in
.I docs/watch-protocol.md
in the AgentGuard checkout.
.PP
The hook centralizes output extraction so agent-specific payload field names do
not leak into local extension policy. It reads output objects, a combined
output string (Codex), and a JSON output envelope string (Muse). The envelope
is unwrapped only when the detected runtime is Muse; its
.B exit_code
then decides whether the command failed, and without one only a
.B terminal_status
of
.B failed
or
.B timed_out
counts as a failure.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AGENTGUARD_WATCH
Set to
.B 0
to stop recording, re-arming, and forgetting watch obligations.
.TP
.B AGENTGUARD_PR_WATCH_HINT
Replaces the advice on how to watch recorded pull requests, here and in the
Stop hook's message.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The post-command checks completed. Credential findings and pull-request
reminders are reported as warnings or reminders rather than blocks.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR agent-hook-pre-bash (1),
.BR agent-hook-stop (1),
.BR git-pr-watch (1)
